# NanoJS8 patch 0002 — JSC dictionary stub.
#
# STATUS: PLACEHOLDER for Phase 0.
# Real .patch is regenerated against actual upstream HEAD by
# tools/apply_gfsk8_patches.ps1 on first clone.
#
# RATIONALE:
# gfsk8-modem-clean ships JSC.cpp with three large static tables:
#   - JSC::prefix[]  (103 entries, ~few KB)
#   - JSC::map[]     (~10,000 string-to-code entries, ~6-8 MB compiled)
#   - JSC::list[]    (~10,000 reverse lookup, ~6-8 MB compiled)
#
# Combined, these tables produce a ~12 MB object file that does not fit in
# our 4 MB factory app partition.
#
# JS8 2.2 explicitly deprecates the JSC compression scheme; Huffman-only
# encoding is the on-the-air default for all modern JS8Call (versions 2.2+).
# NanoJS8 ships Huffman-only and accepts incoming JSC frames as opaque (we
# decode the bit-level frame structure but skip JSC text expansion).
#
# WHAT THE PATCH DOES:
#   - Keeps JSC::prefix[] intact — needed by extendedChars() at decode time
#     for Huffman extended-character handling.
#   - Replaces JSC::map[] with an empty array of the same type.
#   - Replaces JSC::list[] with an empty array of the same type.
#   - Adjusts any size constants that the algorithm derives from list/map size.
#
# RESULT: gfsk8 modem still links and decodes correctly. JSC-compressed
# message bodies are passed to the application as raw 87-bit payloads marked
# as type=JSC; the UI shows "[JSC-encoded message]" and offers no decode.
# Outgoing TX never uses JSC.
#
# EXPECTED DIFF SHAPE (regenerated against actual upstream):
#
#   The patch replaces JSC.cpp wholesale with src/JSC_stub.cpp content (see
#   components/gfsk8_modem/src/JSC_stub.cpp), or applies a sed-style transform
#   of the existing JSC.cpp depending on which approach has lower drift risk
#   against upstream.
#
# WHEN THE REAL .patch IS WRITTEN, IT REPLACES THE TEXT IN THIS FILE.
# THIS PLACEHOLDER MUST NOT BE APPLIED VIA `git apply` — it is documentation.
